{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8893-more-quick-questions-from-me","id":8893,"title":"More quick questions from me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T09:52:11-08:00","id":8893,"title":"More quick questions from me","content":"Actual questions are the important part, text blocks bellow the questions just provide clarification.<br /> <br /> First Question:<br /> Is there some source of a two-way telepathic connection available at character creation?<br /> Specifically: the actual characters I'm planning would be two vampires with the Vampire Spouse merit, who will always be together, but would benefit greatly from full telepathic conversation even w/o Auspex 4 (15th gen can't have 4th level disciplines). But I am likely to re-use various parts of the concept, so the more universal, the better. <br /> Therefore: Merit would be preferable, but something like a Fetish, Wonder, or similar that could be taken with a background would be great too. Something that could / would work for any character type would be best. If the background doesn't work with the character, then that might be able to be passed off with a permissive enough ST (e.g. a vampire with a [cursed] Fetish), so it still counts by me.<br /> <br /> Second Question:<br /> Is there a way to have a vampire be able to absorb 'donated' / spilt blood while in torpor?<br /> Specifically: in a game I am running as ST, there is a cult of a sort who are making sacrifices to a great beast, which is actually a high generation vampire. So long as its hunger is assuaged, it will remain asleep (in torpor), but if it grows too hungry, it will wake to take a banquet of the world (basically, like the 3rd gen is supposed to do, but he's &quot;only&quot; 6th).<br /> I want to make it so that the vampire has a way of taking in the blood from the sacrifices, preferably with the cultists themselves being less than fully aware as to what the creature itself actually is (&quot;<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I\u00e4! I\u00e4! *XX* F</span></span>htagn!&quot; and all that). I would rather do this with something to support it more than just ST fiat / ST custom merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:16:50-08:00","id":8921,"title":"","content":"1) Ascension has the Twin Souls Merit. It's very mage oriented, but it could be a good start for what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> 2) Vampires in torpor can certainly be fed by the rules. The more complicated issue is getting the blood into them. The easiest thing would be for the ritual to involve pouring the blood in a fashion that gets it into the vampire's mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:46:48-08:00","id":8953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8893-more-quick-questions-from-me?p=8921#post8921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Ascension has the Twin Souls Merit. It's very mage oriented, but it could be a good start for what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had actually been looking at that and its counterpart in the Sorcerer rulebook, which work very well for what I want if Mind 1+ or Telepathy 2+ are involved, but not otherwise.<br /> Considering how few Artifacts there are for the Laibon background (the vampire characters both use other things from Ebony Kingdom already), I could probably BS something in that way as a (D&amp;D-esk) pair of rings that allow for the communication, but I want a bit more precedent to build it off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8893-more-quick-questions-from-me?p=8921#post8921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Vampires in torpor can certainly be fed by the rules. The more complicated issue is getting the blood into them. The easiest thing would be for the ritual to involve pouring the blood in a fashion that gets it into the vampire's mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current thought is having the creature (looking quite chthonic due to being of Gangrel blood) look quite cut-up, with the 'cuts' actually being the result of the Thau ritual Stolen Kisses (\u200bBlood Magic p96) made effectively permanent with the ritual Vires Acquirit Eundo (Blood Magic p98). After that I would have the 'demonic creature' (the cult are complete mundanes) be kept in a apparatus like the ones the three elders in Underworld were in.<br /> <br /> But I'm still toying with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}